NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"ai-streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AI Streaming"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Markdown can render the accumulated text of a streamed AI response. Each update parses the complete string synchronously; there is no incremental parser state to coordinate or discard."}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"ai-streaming-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"ai-streaming","data-collapsed-indexes":"[]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/main.tsx\",\"environment\":\"react\",\"files\":{\"/src/main.tsx\":\"import { streamingMarkdownExtension } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming'\\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\\nimport { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\\n\\nconst streamingExtensions = [streamingMarkdownExtension()]\\nconst response = [\\n  '# Release summary',\\n  '',\\n  'The parser safely renders **accumulated text** as it arrives.',\\n  '',\\n  '- No incremental parser state',\\n  '- Incomplete blocks stay predictable',\\n  '',\\n  '```ts',\\n  \\\"const status = 'streaming'\\\",\\n  '```',\\n].join('\\\\n')\\n\\nexport default function Response() {\\n  const [length, setLength] = useState(0)\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (length >= response.length) return\\n    const timeout = window.setTimeout(\\n      () => setLength((value) => value + 1),\\n      18,\\n    )\\n    return () => window.clearTimeout(timeout)\\n  }, [length])\\n\\n  return (\\n    <main>\\n      <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={() => setLength(0)}>\\n        Replay\\n      </button>\\n      <Markdown\\n        extensions={streamingExtensions}\\n        frontmatter={false}\\n        headingIds={false}\\n      >\\n        {response.slice(0, length)}\\n      </Markdown>\\n    </main>\\n  )\\n}\\n\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { streamingMarkdownExtension } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming'\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\nimport { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\n\nconst streamingExtensions = [streamingMarkdownExtension()]\nconst response = [\n  '# Release summary',\n  '',\n  'The parser safely renders **accumulated text** as it arrives.',\n  '',\n  '- No incremental parser state',\n  '- Incomplete blocks stay predictable',\n  '',\n  '```ts',\n  \"const status = 'streaming'\",\n  '```',\n].join('\\n')\n\nexport default function Response() {\n  const [length, setLength] = useState(0)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (length >= response.length) return\n    const timeout = window.setTimeout(\n      () => setLength((value) => value + 1),\n      18,\n    )\n    return () => window.clearTimeout(timeout)\n  }, [length])\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => setLength(0)}>\n        Replay\n      </button>\n      <Markdown\n        extensions={streamingExtensions}\n        frontmatter={false}\n        headingIds={false}\n      >\n        {response.slice(0, length)}\n      </Markdown>\n    </main>\n  )\n}\n","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=ai-streaming env=react file=/src/main.tsx entry","title":"/src/main.tsx","file":"/src/main.tsx"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The streaming extension suppresses empty trailing headings, blockquotes, and list items while a response is incomplete. It does not change completed paragraphs, lists, tables, quotes, or fenced code. An unclosed code fence renders all code accumulated after its opening fence."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the extension enabled after completion unless an intentionally empty final heading, quote, or list item is meaningful in your application. Without the extension, core parsing preserves those valid Markdown structures."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"partial-inline-syntax","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Partial inline syntax"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unclosed emphasis, code spans, links, and other inline delimiters remain literal text until their closing delimiter arrives. Completing a table delimiter, list continuation, or inline construct can legitimately restructure the latest block."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The package reparses the accumulated response rather than maintaining parser state between updates. Batch very small transport tokens into normal UI updates when responses are unusually long or tokens arrive faster than the screen should repaint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With the streaming extension enabled, React keeps completed groups of plain code lines in stable text nodes. Appending code updates the trailing group instead of replacing the entire block's text, which reduces browser layout work. Custom code components still receive string children, and highlighters keep their existing HTML rendering path."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"security","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AI output is untrusted content:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"leave "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowHtml"},{"type":"text","value":" disabled"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"use only highlighters that escape source code"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"apply application policies to outbound links and remote images"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"use component overrides when links or images need custom behavior"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Executable URL protocols are removed and raw HTML is escaped by default. The streaming extension does not relax those policies."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable frontmatter for AI responses so a completed closing delimiter cannot reinterpret the beginning of a response as metadata. Disabling heading IDs also avoids changing an element ID each time a streamed heading grows."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"html-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTML rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same profile works without React:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { streamingMarkdownExtension } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml(accumulatedResponse, {\n  extensions: [streamingMarkdownExtension()],\n  frontmatter: false,\n  headingIds: false,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTML and React output are tested for structural parity at every character boundary across representative prose, links, lists, tables, quotes, code, raw HTML, and executable URLs."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"ai-streaming","text":"AI Streaming","level":1},{"id":"partial-inline-syntax","text":"Partial inline syntax","level":2},{"id":"security","text":"Security","level":2},{"id":"html-rendering","text":"HTML rendering","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# AI Streaming\n\nTanStack Markdown can render the accumulated text of a streamed AI response. Each update parses the complete string synchronously; there is no incremental parser state to coordinate or discard.\n\n```tsx group=ai-streaming env=react file=/src/main.tsx entry\nimport { streamingMarkdownExtension } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming'\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\nimport { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\n\nconst streamingExtensions = [streamingMarkdownExtension()]\nconst response = [\n  '# Release summary',\n  '',\n  'The parser safely renders **accumulated text** as it arrives.',\n  '',\n  '- No incremental parser state',\n  '- Incomplete blocks stay predictable',\n  '',\n  '```ts',\n  \"const status = 'streaming'\",\n  '```',\n].join('\\n')\n\nexport default function Response() {\n  const [length, setLength] = useState(0)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (length >= response.length) return\n    const timeout = window.setTimeout(\n      () => setLength((value) => value + 1),\n      18,\n    )\n    return () => window.clearTimeout(timeout)\n  }, [length])\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => setLength(0)}>\n        Replay\n      </button>\n      <Markdown\n        extensions={streamingExtensions}\n        frontmatter={false}\n        headingIds={false}\n      >\n        {response.slice(0, length)}\n      </Markdown>\n    </main>\n  )\n}\n\n```\n\nThe streaming extension suppresses empty trailing headings, blockquotes, and list items while a response is incomplete. It does not change completed paragraphs, lists, tables, quotes, or fenced code. An unclosed code fence renders all code accumulated after its opening fence.\n\nKeep the extension enabled after completion unless an intentionally empty final heading, quote, or list item is meaningful in your application. Without the extension, core parsing preserves those valid Markdown structures.\n\n## Partial inline syntax\n\nUnclosed emphasis, code spans, links, and other inline delimiters remain literal text until their closing delimiter arrives. Completing a table delimiter, list continuation, or inline construct can legitimately restructure the latest block.\n\nThe package reparses the accumulated response rather than maintaining parser state between updates. Batch very small transport tokens into normal UI updates when responses are unusually long or tokens arrive faster than the screen should repaint.\n\nWith the streaming extension enabled, React keeps completed groups of plain code lines in stable text nodes. Appending code updates the trailing group instead of replacing the entire block's text, which reduces browser layout work. Custom code components still receive string children, and highlighters keep their existing HTML rendering path.\n\n## Security\n\nAI output is untrusted content:\n\n- leave `allowHtml` disabled\n- use only highlighters that escape source code\n- apply application policies to outbound links and remote images\n- use component overrides when links or images need custom behavior\n\nExecutable URL protocols are removed and raw HTML is escaped by default. The streaming extension does not relax those policies.\n\nDisable frontmatter for AI responses so a completed closing delimiter cannot reinterpret the beginning of a response as metadata. Disabling heading IDs also avoids changing an element ID each time a streamed heading grows.\n\n## HTML rendering\n\nThe same profile works without React:\n\n```ts\nimport { streamingMarkdownExtension } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml(accumulatedResponse, {\n  extensions: [streamingMarkdownExtension()],\n  frontmatter: false,\n  headingIds: false,\n})\n```\n\nHTML and React output are tested for structural parity at every character boundary across representative prose, links, lists, tables, quotes, code, raw HTML, and executable URLs.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: AI Streaming\n---\n\n# AI Streaming\n\nTanStack Markdown can render the accumulated text of a streamed AI response. Each update parses the complete string synchronously; there is no incremental parser state to coordinate or discard.\n\n```tsx group=ai-streaming env=react file=/src/main.tsx entry\nimport { streamingMarkdownExtension } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming'\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\nimport { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\n\nconst streamingExtensions = [streamingMarkdownExtension()]\nconst response = [\n  '# Release summary',\n  '',\n  'The parser safely renders **accumulated text** as it arrives.',\n  '',\n  '- No incremental parser state',\n  '- Incomplete blocks stay predictable',\n  '',\n  '```ts',\n  \"const status = 'streaming'\",\n  '```',\n].join('\\n')\n\nexport default function Response() {\n  const [length, setLength] = useState(0)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (length >= response.length) return\n    const timeout = window.setTimeout(\n      () => setLength((value) => value + 1),\n      18,\n    )\n    return () => window.clearTimeout(timeout)\n  }, [length])\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => setLength(0)}>\n        Replay\n      </button>\n      <Markdown\n        extensions={streamingExtensions}\n        frontmatter={false}\n        headingIds={false}\n      >\n        {response.slice(0, length)}\n      </Markdown>\n    </main>\n  )\n}\n\n```\n\nThe streaming extension suppresses empty trailing headings, blockquotes, and list items while a response is incomplete. It does not change completed paragraphs, lists, tables, quotes, or fenced code. An unclosed code fence renders all code accumulated after its opening fence.\n\nKeep the extension enabled after completion unless an intentionally empty final heading, quote, or list item is meaningful in your application. Without the extension, core parsing preserves those valid Markdown structures.\n\n## Partial inline syntax\n\nUnclosed emphasis, code spans, links, and other inline delimiters remain literal text until their closing delimiter arrives. Completing a table delimiter, list continuation, or inline construct can legitimately restructure the latest block.\n\nThe package reparses the accumulated response rather than maintaining parser state between updates. Batch very small transport tokens into normal UI updates when responses are unusually long or tokens arrive faster than the screen should repaint.\n\nWith the streaming extension enabled, React keeps completed groups of plain code lines in stable text nodes. Appending code updates the trailing group instead of replacing the entire block's text, which reduces browser layout work. Custom code components still receive string children, and highlighters keep their existing HTML rendering path.\n\n## Security\n\nAI output is untrusted content:\n\n- leave `allowHtml` disabled\n- use only highlighters that escape source code\n- apply application policies to outbound links and remote images\n- use component overrides when links or images need custom behavior\n\nExecutable URL protocols are removed and raw HTML is escaped by default. The streaming extension does not relax those policies.\n\nDisable frontmatter for AI responses so a completed closing delimiter cannot reinterpret the beginning of a response as metadata. Disabling heading IDs also avoids changing an element ID each time a streamed heading grows.\n\n## HTML rendering\n\nThe same profile works without React:\n\n```ts\nimport { streamingMarkdownExtension } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml(accumulatedResponse, {\n  extensions: [streamingMarkdownExtension()],\n  frontmatter: false,\n  headingIds: false,\n})\n```\n\nHTML and React output are tested for structural parity at every character boundary across representative prose, links, lists, tables, quotes, code, raw HTML, and executable URLs.\n"}
